module xiom.format.relative

// ============================================================================
// Human-readable relative time: "5 minutes ago", "in 2 days", elapsed and
// remaining durations, ages, and decomposed relative-time parts. Pure
// computation over integer timestamps with zero external dependencies.
// ============================================================================

// fn format_relative_time(seconds: Int) -> Str - format a signed offset in seconds as a full relative phrase. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_relative_time_short(seconds: Int) -> Str - format a signed offset using the compact unit form (e.g. "5m"). TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_relative_future(seconds: Int) -> Str - format a positive offset as "in N units". TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_relative_past(seconds: Int) -> Str - format a negative offset as "N units ago". TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_elapsed(start: Int, end: Int) -> Str - format the span between two timestamps as elapsed time. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_elapsed_ms(ms: Int) -> Str - format a millisecond span as a compact human duration. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_ago(timestamp: Int, now: Int) -> Str - format how long before now the timestamp lies. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_until(timestamp: Int, now: Int) -> Str - format how long after now the timestamp lies. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn format_age(days: Int) -> Str - format an age in days as the largest whole unit. TODO(compiler): implement.
// fn relative_parts(seconds: Int) -> Vec[(Int, Str)] - decompose seconds into (magnitude, unit) pairs from largest to smallest. TODO(compiler): implement.
